.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt PKGBASE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkgbase
.Nd FreeBSD upgrade tool in PKGBASE world similar to freebsd-update(8) command.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm help
.Nm
.Cm upgrade -r
.Ar VERSION
.Op Fl L
.Op Fl B
.Nm
.Cm loader
.Nm
.Cm pkgnew
.Nm
.Cm modules
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm 
is a upgrade tool in FreeBSD PKGBASE world, similar to
.Xr freebsd-update 8
command.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The 
.Nm
utility implements updating of a pkgbase FreeBSD system similar to the
.Xr freebsd-update 8
did for non-pkgbase FreeBSD systems. It automates the upgrade and update of the FreeBSD system and uses
.Xr bectl 8
for boot-environment creation for ZFS based systems. It also handles the UEFI/BIOS bootcode upgrade.
.Nm 
can also be used to do upgrade inside a jail.
.Ss Supported Subcommands and Flags
.Bl -tag -width indent

.It Xo
.Cm help
.Xc
.br
Print usage information and exit.
.It Xo
.Cm upgrade
.Fl r Ar VERSION
.Op Fl L
.Op Fl B
.Xc
.br
Upgrade the system to a new FreeBSD release. The
.Ar VERSION
string expects the format of the FreeBSD release string. e.g. 15.1-RELEASE or 15.2-BETA2. The -L flag omits upgrading the UEFI/BIOS bootcode. Flag -B omits creating a ZFS Boot Environment, default for UFS based systems.
.It Xo
.Cm loader
.Xc
.br
Runs only the UEFI/BIOS bootcode upgrade.
.It Xo
.Cm pkgnew
.Xc
.br
Check for config files with .pkgnew suffix. If any files will be listed, manually check them with
.Xr diff 1
and merge any necessary changes.
.It Xo
.Cm modules
.Xc
.br
Check for 3rd party kmods installed from packages.
.It Xo
.Cm version
.Xc
.br
Print pkgbase version and exit.
.Sh EXAMPLES
To upgrade the system to FreeBSD 15.2-BETA2 run:
.Pp
.Dl pkgbase upgrade -r 15.2-BETA2
.Pp
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr freebsd-update 3 ,
.Xr bectl 8,
.Xr zfs 8,
.Xr gpart 8
